WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:00.834
If Russia's latest

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.710
offensive in Ukraine

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.712
is, in fact, underway, senior U.S.

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:05.797
officials are not impressed.

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:06.673
Have a listen.

00:00:07.966 --> 00:00:10.010
Russia continue to introduce

00:00:11.553 --> 00:00:13.805
large numbers of troops into

00:00:14.222 --> 00:00:15.974
into the theater.

00:00:15.974 --> 00:00:17.517
Those troops are

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.686
ill equipped and ill trained

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.770
And because of that,

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:22.856
they're incurring a lot of casualties.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.984
And we expect that that will continue

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:28.778
Russia has declared that it is

00:00:29.988 --> 00:00:31.865
launching a new offensive.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:35.285
Well, if this is it, it is very pathetic.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.496
I would say the latter.

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:39.914
I spoke with CNN military analyst

00:00:39.914 --> 00:00:40.749
Cedric Leighton

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:42.125
for his take on the modern

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:43.001
Russian military.

00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:43.793
Here he is

00:00:45.295 --> 00:00:46.880
It's very interesting, John.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.297
So, you know,

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:47.964
for those of us

00:00:47.964 --> 00:00:49.299
who've been watching the Russians

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:50.550
for some time,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.720
a lot of the things that we learned

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.096
or thought we knew about them

00:00:55.096 --> 00:00:58.183
involved large numbers, a new doctrine,

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.727
new weapons systems thing

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.104
that really could change

00:01:03.104 --> 00:01:05.023
the course of warfare itself.

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:06.858
Not just the tactical action,

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:08.985
but the whole strategy of warfare.

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:11.905
And, you know, barring any unforeseen

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:15.408
developments, it looks as if the Russians

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.160
are not able to mount

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.536
the kind of offensive

00:01:18.536 --> 00:01:19.746
that their doctrine promised

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:20.497
we would see that

00:01:20.497 --> 00:01:21.998
their weapons systems promised

00:01:21.998 --> 00:01:22.874
we would see,

00:01:22.874 --> 00:01:24.542
and that the rhetoric promise

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:25.376
that we would see

00:01:25.376 --> 00:01:28.046
that none of that is coming to pass.

00:01:28.296 --> 00:01:30.131
And it seems as if we are dealing

00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:32.300
with a paper tiger, in essence.

00:01:33.134 --> 00:01:34.636
There is also this reporting

00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:36.513
we have from The New York Times.

00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:37.597
As Moscow steps up

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.307
its offensive in eastern Ukraine,

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:40.517
weeks of failed attacks

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:42.060
on the Ukrainian stronghold

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:42.852
have left two

00:01:42.852 --> 00:01:44.562
Russian brigades in tatters.

00:01:44.562 --> 00:01:45.188
Raised questions

00:01:45.188 --> 00:01:46.481
about Russia's military tactics

00:01:46.481 --> 00:01:48.024
and renewed doubts about its ability

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:49.901
to maintain sustained large scale

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.486
ground assault, as you were saying.

00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:52.028
Now, the town is

00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:53.696
Volodya is not far from bombed

00:01:53.696 --> 00:01:54.697
which is a city

00:01:54.697 --> 00:01:56.324
of no real strategic value.

00:01:56.324 --> 00:01:57.367
It is a symbolic importance,

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.410
but no strategic value to two.

00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:00.870
So in tatters

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.997
in terms of losses, how big is that?

00:02:02.997 --> 00:02:04.541
And it would seem to be like high costs.

00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:05.416
A little reward here.

00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:07.377
Yes.

00:02:07.377 --> 00:02:09.671
So that is a really significant thing.

00:02:09.712 --> 00:02:11.214
These two brigades in question,

00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:14.092
the one 55th and the 40th Marine

00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:15.343
Infantry Brigade or Naval

00:02:15.343 --> 00:02:17.762
Infantry Brigade of the Russian

00:02:18.096 --> 00:02:20.890
naval forces of the Pacific Fleet.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:23.309
Those are fairly large elements.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.270
So we're talking somewhere around 2000

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:28.523
to 3500 or so personnel

00:02:29.107 --> 00:02:31.151
that are just gone.

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:34.487
And what you're dealing with here is a

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:38.032
systematic neglect of the entire system.

00:02:38.616 --> 00:02:40.243
And it seems that this neglect

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:42.245
has been going on for quite some time.

00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:43.329
But it has been papered

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:46.207
over by every level of command

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.293
in the Russian military until,

00:02:48.293 --> 00:02:48.793
of course,

00:02:48.793 --> 00:02:52.422
these brigades are put into action.

00:02:52.422 --> 00:02:54.132
And they can't perform

00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:55.008
the military missions

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.509
that they've been assigned.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.511
So this is a significant issue

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.345
because

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.139
every time these brigades

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:02.932
move into combat,

00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:04.058
they move with less and less

00:03:04.058 --> 00:03:06.394
people, less and less armament,

00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:08.021
and they're far less capable

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.148
than they originally were supposed to be.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:12.066
U.S.

00:03:12.066 --> 00:03:12.317
U.S.

00:03:12.317 --> 00:03:12.775
appears to be

00:03:12.775 --> 00:03:14.402
shifting to a long term approach

00:03:14.402 --> 00:03:15.195
of fighting Ukraine

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:17.197
with military supplies and weapons.

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.740
Officials say it's time to look beyond

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.200
what Ukraine needs now,

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.367
such as Abrams tanks,

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.077
which the US has promised to deliver,

00:03:23.077 --> 00:03:23.870
and to look into what

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.747
Ukraine will need in the long run

00:03:25.747 --> 00:03:27.248
to deter any possible future

00:03:27.248 --> 00:03:29.542
aggressive moves by Moscow.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:30.877
Meanwhile, the ongoing war is

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:33.004
exhausting NATO's ammunition stockpiles.

00:03:33.254 --> 00:03:34.631
CNN's Art Levine reports.

00:03:34.631 --> 00:03:34.839
U.S.

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:35.673
defense factories

00:03:35.673 --> 00:03:38.801
are preparing to ramp up production

00:03:41.471 --> 00:03:42.180
in the steel

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.224
furnaces of Scranton, Pennsylvania.

00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:46.935
The weapons of war are in high demand.

00:03:47.018 --> 00:03:50.063
One tonne metal rods heated and forged

00:03:51.522 --> 00:03:53.524
in to about 11,000 high

00:03:53.524 --> 00:03:55.568
explosive artillery shells a month.

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:57.779
CNN got a rare

00:03:57.779 --> 00:03:59.155
look inside the Scranton

00:03:59.155 --> 00:04:01.491
Army ammunition plant,

00:04:01.491 --> 00:04:03.034
one of only a few in the country

00:04:03.034 --> 00:04:05.578
that make this crucial round here

00:04:05.828 --> 00:04:07.163
especially made steels

00:04:07.163 --> 00:04:09.958
heated to 2000 degrees, slowly shaped.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.044
Step by scorching step

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:16.256
into its final product.

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:16.923
To this point,

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:17.257
it's only

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.842
taken a few hours to heat the steel

00:04:19.842 --> 00:04:21.135
and then to turn it into what

00:04:21.135 --> 00:04:22.053
looks like

00:04:22.053 --> 00:04:23.012
an artillery shell

00:04:23.012 --> 00:04:25.098
compressed into that familiar shape.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.891
But it's still days of testing

00:04:26.891 --> 00:04:27.725
and inspections

00:04:27.725 --> 00:04:28.226
to make sure

00:04:28.226 --> 00:04:29.686
that this can be turned

00:04:29.686 --> 00:04:32.063
into a 155 millimeter artillery shell

00:04:32.313 --> 00:04:34.732
that can be fired from the field.

00:04:34.732 --> 00:04:37.235
The process doesn't end here.

00:04:37.235 --> 00:04:38.486
The empty shells are shipped

00:04:38.486 --> 00:04:40.113
to another plant for explosives.

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.155
Fuzes.

00:04:41.155 --> 00:04:42.323
5000 miles

00:04:42.323 --> 00:04:44.325
from the front lines and mother Russia.

00:04:44.409 --> 00:04:47.412
The enemy here is Father Time, forced to

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.706
Ukraine can burn through the plant's

00:04:49.706 --> 00:04:52.000
monthly production in half a week,

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.835
locked in a grinding war of attrition

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:55.003
with Putin's army

00:04:55.003 --> 00:04:56.504
and Russian mercenaries.

00:04:56.504 --> 00:04:59.048
The current rate of Ukraine's ammunition

00:04:59.048 --> 00:05:02.969
expenditure is many times higher than our

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.846
current rate of production.

00:05:06.347 --> 00:05:06.848
One year

00:05:06.848 --> 00:05:07.807
in the war has

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:09.851
turned into a vicious math problem

00:05:09.851 --> 00:05:10.852
how to make enough ammo

00:05:10.852 --> 00:05:11.894
for Ukraine,

00:05:11.894 --> 00:05:13.938
the United States and allies.

00:05:13.938 --> 00:05:14.981
The Pentagon is already

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.941
planning on new ammo plans in Texas.

00:05:16.941 --> 00:05:17.859
And Canada,

00:05:17.859 --> 00:05:18.568
part of a race

00:05:18.568 --> 00:05:20.320
to increase the capacity of the defense

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.612
industrial base.

00:05:21.612 --> 00:05:22.322
Doug Bush

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.365
is the Army's head of acquisitions.

00:05:24.365 --> 00:05:27.076
Right now we are meeting demand

00:05:27.076 --> 00:05:27.827
I of course,

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.370
I would want it to be faster.

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:30.997
Everyone does.

00:05:31.247 --> 00:05:32.915
But there's a time factor.

00:05:32.915 --> 00:05:33.916
A year to 18 months

00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:35.501
is often what you're looking at.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.545
Bush says this is the greatest ramp

00:05:37.545 --> 00:05:39.672
up in military production,

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.924
possibly going back to the Korean War.

00:05:41.924 --> 00:05:42.925
Early on, we realized

00:05:42.925 --> 00:05:44.385
we had to really put our foot

00:05:44.385 --> 00:05:45.762
all the way to the floor.

00:05:45.762 --> 00:05:47.805
The goal within two years is to produce

00:05:47.805 --> 00:05:48.556
five times

00:05:48.556 --> 00:05:50.350
more artillery rounds each month, up

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.809
to 70,000.

00:05:51.809 --> 00:05:54.103
Twice as many Javelin anti-tank missiles.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:55.605
Up to 4000 a month.

00:05:55.605 --> 00:05:56.898
30% more rounds

00:05:56.898 --> 00:05:58.691
for the high Mars rocket launchers.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.276
About eight 50 a month.

00:06:01.903 --> 00:06:02.653
Precision weapon.

00:06:02.653 --> 00:06:03.196
Ukraine is

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:03.780
used to target

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.948
Russian command posts and ammo depots.

00:06:06.407 --> 00:06:08.743
And 60 Stinger anti-aircraft missiles

00:06:08.743 --> 00:06:09.952
each month.

00:06:09.952 --> 00:06:12.080
The US isn't at war with Russia,

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:13.289
but that matters little

00:06:13.289 --> 00:06:14.874
to weapons manufacturers

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.834
whose products are part of the fight.

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:18.795
Our defense industrial base

00:06:18.795 --> 00:06:20.713
is still largely

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:23.299
geared towards a peacetime environment

00:06:23.633 --> 00:06:25.718
and not towards a wartime

00:06:25.802 --> 00:06:27.845
or at least a quasi wartime environment

00:06:27.845 --> 00:06:30.264
that we're now in.

00:06:30.264 --> 00:06:32.517
To get a sense of just how much the Army

00:06:32.517 --> 00:06:33.810
is investing in this.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:35.019
Within the last couple of weeks,

00:06:35.019 --> 00:06:35.812
the Army has announced

00:06:35.812 --> 00:06:36.145
one and a

00:06:36.145 --> 00:06:37.271
half billion dollars

00:06:37.271 --> 00:06:38.147
in procurement

00:06:38.147 --> 00:06:40.858
of new 155 millimeter artillery rounds.

00:06:41.025 --> 00:06:42.068
They're trying to produce

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:43.945
this crucial ammunition faster

00:06:43.945 --> 00:06:46.030
and then trying to produce more of it.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:48.032
Oren Liebermann, CNN, at the Pentagon.

